{"t": 503.955, "n": 204, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I fixed the three reviewer points and rewrote the hand-off to match. I couldn't run the structure check or git here, so the gate decides whether the specs pass.\n\n- **LIF-B17, first scenario:** the task's version is gone. The scenario now uses an invented `claude` 2.4.0 (inside the table) and 2.5.0 (above its `range`). The behaviour sentence names the engine and the compatibility table instead.\n- **LIF-AC12:** it is now stated as the rule: for each executor of the compatibility table, a version its facts name as confirmed is in `recorded` and inside `range`, and preflight on it raises no `executor-version-untested` warning. \"The shipped compatibility table\" is gone.\n- **ECC-B24 and ECC-AC19:** \"second turn\" is gone. P-CC-13 passes only when the probe has read the tools offered or the context size at every turn of a session of more than one turn, launched as ECC-B18 and ECC-B20 say, and each reading shows no tool of an undeclared server. This restores the rule ECC-B13 had before (\"in every turn\") in checkable form. The scenarios say \"a later turn\", and the figures and the turn they appear at belong to the L-43 rows and the live test.\n\nSizes, measured with an anchored byte-count regex in Grep:\n- **`executor-claude-code.spec.md`:** exactly 30,149 bytes and 214 lines, 571 bytes under the limit. A later change to it must first split the MCP isolation behaviours (ECC-B18 to ECC-B24) into their own spec.\n- **`lifecycle-and-evals.spec.md`:** under 20,000 bytes.\n\nI checked that each new id is defined once, that every criterion names its behaviour, and that the added lines carry no task-tied wording. I re-read the code behind ECC-B21 to ECC-B23 (`claude.py:395-446`, `mcpconfig.py:45-61` and `135-142`, `preflight.py:78-173`). The neighbouring specs it links (EXI-B1, EXI-B17, TSA-B12, SEC-B3, WSP-B5) do not contradict it.\n\nThe hand-off covers G1 to G4, the decisions, the inferred behaviours and the reading list.\n- **Open question for the owner:** the data fix needs `range` widened to `>=2.1.329,<=2.1.332`. That also makes 2.1.330 and 2.1.331 read as recorded, although the runbook (line 76) leaves `executor_compat.json` alone until the owner accepts the container as a place of record. The default is to widen; the alternative is to let `recorded` alone decide, which changes LIF-B10 and the table code.\n- **Reported, not fixed:** ECC-B13's sentence was already far over 500 characters. My edit shortens it, and I did not split it.\n- **Left to the plan:** the two L-43 runbook rows, because discovery writes no plan.\n\nARTIFACT handoff: plugins/tempergraph/docs/tasks/i21b.handoff.md", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "5e62f5f4-a46f-4e45-b352-06da3954f7ce"}
